-- ============================================================================
-- DR12 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Well Cost & Time, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE MONEY. Turning the days and metres the tier below
-- produced into an authority for expenditure, which is a request for
-- permission with a number attached rather than a forecast.
--
-- EVERY LINE CARRIES TWO INDEPENDENT ANSWERS: a BASIS, which says how it
-- bills, and a CATEGORY, which says what kind of spend it is. Getting the
-- basis right and the category wrong moves the tangible and intangible split
-- without touching the total, so the estimate looks correct while the sheet is
-- wrong in the place a tax treatment reads.
--
-- THE SHARPEST RESULT IN THE TIER IS ABOUT EXPOSURE. The same money calibrated
-- three ways bills IDENTICALLY at the base case and diverges the moment
-- anything moves: elasticity to elapsed days is 1 for a per-day line and 0 for
-- per-metre and lump. On the published estimate 53.53 percent of the base is
-- per-day exposed, so one extra day costs 160,000 dollars that stops being
-- negotiable the moment the well is spudded. Deepening the hole is the MIRROR
-- case, where per-metre moves faster than per-day, because the day count
-- carries flat time that does not grow with depth. A line put on the wrong
-- basis prices correctly today and reprices wrongly forever after.
--
-- CONTINGENCY IS A PROVISION THAT CAN OUTRANK A CONTRACT. It sits on the BASE
-- and not the total, and it passes any given line at a fraction equal to that
-- line's share of the base, so the general condition is f > L / base. On the
-- published estimate it passes the largest contracted line at 0.3346 and the
-- second at 0.2007, and even at 10 percent it already ranks fourth of nine. A
-- percentage is not an answer until you know which percentile it reaches,
-- which is the question the Expert tier takes up.
--
-- AND COST PER METRE CAN RANK SECTIONS DIFFERENTLY FROM TOTAL SPEND. Sweeping
-- the intermediate section's rate shows a disagreement band between 9.03 and
-- 14.42 metres an hour where a longer, faster section costs LESS per metre and
-- MORE in total. The published well drills it at 15, just outside, so the two
-- rankings agree there but only just.
--
-- ONE PROVENANCE RULE THE TIER STATES OUT LOUD: a cost per metre must be
-- computed from the hours of the section it belongs to. The 770 dollars per
-- metre figure in the fixtures is a standalone worked example whose trip time
-- matches no trip in the published schedule, and no lesson presents it as a
-- section's own number.
-- ============================================================================

values ('wellcost', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-an-afe-is-a-structure","title":"An AFE Is a Structure","lesson_keys":["l01-what-an-afe-is-for","l02-line-items","l03-two-classifications-at-once","l04-what-the-engine-needs-from-you"]},{"key":"m02-the-three-cost-bases","title":"The Three Cost Bases","lesson_keys":["l01-per-day","l02-per-metre","l03-lump","l04-which-basis-fits-which-line","l05-a-basis-chosen-wrong"]},{"key":"m03-tangible-and-intangible","title":"Tangible and Intangible","lesson_keys":["l01-the-split","l02-what-decides-which","l03-why-anyone-cares","l04-reading-a-sorted-afe","l05-the-split-is-not-a-quality-judgement"]},{"key":"m04-contingency","title":"Contingency","lesson_keys":["l01-a-provision-not-a-cost","l02-where-it-sits","l03-a-provision-can-outrank-a-contract","l04-what-a-percentage-actually-buys"]},{"key":"m05-cost-per-metre","title":"Cost Per Metre","lesson_keys":["l01-the-form","l02-the-hours-it-needs","l03-the-interval-it-divides-by","l04-the-inversion","l05-what-it-is-good-for"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'wellcost' and tier = 'intermediate';

